#use(std/rfc2119)

#rfc2119-boilerplate

Even when the FIRST reference to a keyword occurs inside an ##xref-scope
(so the collect-time registration runs under that scope), the RFC keywords are
a global vocabulary and resolve everywhere.

#xref-scope(name: "impl")
	Inside the scope, the server #ref('must) validate the token.

	#def("token"){token}{an opaque credential}

	Refer to the #ref("token") here.

Back at root, the client #ref('should) retry; the scoped token def is
NOT visible here, but the RFC keywords still are: it #ref('may) cache.
